#% title
# kurtosis

#% text
# `kurtosis(d)` gives the kurtosis `E[(X - mu)^4]/sigma^4` of a distribution, 3 for a normal one; `kurtosis(xs)` gives `m4/m2^2` of a data list.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
kurtosis(normal_distribution(mu, s))
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
kurtosis(exponential_distribution(l))
#% output
#= 9

#% cell
kurtosis([1, 2, 3, 4, 100])
#% output
#= 18802417/5791210

